                   Parameters for FLUVSIM
                   **********************

START OF PARAMETERS:
well58c.dat                      -file with well conditioning data
0  1  2  3  4                  -  columns for well #, X, Y, Z, facies
-1.0      1.0e21              -  trimming limits
0                              -debugging level: 0,1,2,3
well58c.dbg                    -file for debugging output
well58c.geo                    -file for geometric specification
seiswell58c.out                       -file for simulation output
well58c.vp                     -file for vertical prop curve output
well58c.ap                     -file for areal prop map output
seiswell58c.wd                        -file for well data output
1                              -number of realizations to generate
100   326000.0    50.0
100   9350000.0   50.0               -ny,ymn,ysiz - geological coordinates
66          66.0               -nz, average thickness in physical units
94204411                          -random number seed
1   0   1   1                  -1=on,0=off: global, vert, areal, wells
1.0  1.  0.5  1.                 -weighting : global, vert, areal, wells
5000    1000   0.1                -maximum iter, max no change, min. obj.
0.0   0.10   5  7  10           -annealing schedule: t0,redfac,ka,k,num
0.5 0.1 0.1 0.3                -Pert prob: 1on+1off, 1on, 1off, fix well
   1    0    0                 -Facies(on): channel, levee, crevasse
0.20 0.28 0.0                  -Proportion: channel, levee, crevasse
pcurve.dat                     -  vertical proportion curves
0                              -     0=net-to-gross, 1=all facies
1  7  8                        -     column numbers
seis58cprop.dat                  -  areal proportion map
0                              -     0=net-to-gross, 1=all facies
1  3  4                        -     column numbers
199                               -maximum number of channels
-10     0       10              - orientation of the channel
100.0  300.0   500.0             -channel:  sinuosity: average departure
3000.0  4000.0   5000.0           -channel:  sinuosity: length scale
  2.0    5.0     20.0           -channel:  thickness
  1.0    1.0     1.0           -channel:  thickness undulation
1000.0  1000.0   1000.0           -channel:  thickness undul. length scale
20.0  40.0    60.0              -channel:  width/thickness ratio
  1.0    1.0     1.0           -channel:  width: undulation
500.0  1000.0   1500.0           -channel:  width: undulation length scale
100.0  500.0   1000.0           -levee:    average width
  0.1    0.1     0.1           -levee:    average height
  0.2    0.4     0.6           -levee:    depth below top
 80.0   80.0    80.0           -crevasse: attachment length
  0.25   0.5     0.75          -crevasse: relative thickness by channel
500.0  500.0   500.0           -crevasse: areal size (diameter)
